% What happens between two runs of the rules: the Java driver's inserts and deletes, as events in the world.
when the fire in a room is put out
then it is not the case that there is a fire in the room.

when a fire starts in a room
then there is a fire in the room.

initially there is a room called kitchen
    and there is a room called bedroom
    and there is a room called office
    and there is a room called livingroom
    and there is a sprinkler in kitchen
    and there is a sprinkler in bedroom
    and there is a sprinkler in office
    and there is a sprinkler in livingroom.

% Drools (a KieSession on the same working memory and steps) fired 11 rule(s) and ended with
% (its facts as this twin's fluents):
%   - room(bedroom)
%   - room(kitchen)
%   - room(livingroom)
%   - room(office)
%   - sprinkler(bedroom)
%   - sprinkler(kitchen)
%   - sprinkler(livingroom)
%   - sprinkler(office)
% The twin's final state under LPS2 (`lps state`) is compared with it by test_drools.pl.
scenario driver is:
    % the driver's step 1 (then the rules run again)
    a fire starts in kitchen from 10 to 11.
    a fire starts in office from 10 to 11.
    % the driver's step 2 (then the rules run again)
    the fire in kitchen is put out from 20 to 21.
    the fire in office is put out from 20 to 21.

